---
// src/pages/_site-updates/2026-08-24-waitlist-confirmation-email.astro
export const updateMeta = {
  date: '2026-08-24',
  title: 'Waitlist applicants receive a personal confirmation email',
  tags: ['email', 'waitlist', 'lead-capture'],
};
---
<article class="border-l-4 border-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] pl-6">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">August 24, 2026</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
    Submitting the waitlist application at
    <a href="/pricing" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/pricing</a> now sends the
    applicant a branded confirmation email carrying both founders' direct addresses.
  </p>

  <div class="mb-4">
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Why</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
      Under invitation-only access this email is the first real contact in a relationship that
      continues one to one, so it reads as a note from two people rather than a transactional
      receipt. It says the application was received, that breeders are onboarded one at a time,
      and that either founder can be written to directly in the meantime.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-4">
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">How it works</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
      The <code>launch_waitlist</code> source was added to the existing auto-reply opt-in set in
      <code>leadCapture.ts</code>, reusing the branded template already used for other opted-in
      sources: BreederHQ logo, brand-orange header, and a highlighted panel. Source-specific
      replies take precedence over interest-derived ones, because the waitlist form sends a species
      in the interest field and would otherwise have selected a generic follow-up and buried the
      personal note. The subject line, intro, panel heading, and the label above the contact
      buttons all branch on source, in both the HTML and the plain-text alternative. Replies route
      to a founder rather than the shared inbox.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Also corrected</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
      Two auto-reply follow-ups still offered a "Create a free account" link into self-serve
      registration, which no longer exists for breeders; both now point at the waitlist. The dog
      show reply no longer references a free year, since that booth offer has ended.
    </p>
  </div>
</article>
